    "reasoning": "All 14 field answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. The source error is confined to q-86869: its factorial expansion contains the authored fragment '6\\times 5\\times \\times 3', omitting 4 and leaving consecutive multiplication signs; its final answer 720 is correct. Independently: q-86869 has 6!=720 assignments; q-102894 has 6!-1=719 permutations besides BINARY. q-26811 is increasing with intercept (0,5) and asymptote y=4; q-26815 is increasing with intercept (0,0.25) and asymptote y=-0.75. These features identify the current graph choices and agree with the captured transformations. For q-7230 and q-7232, the asymptotes give c=-2 and c=-3 respectively; substituting these source-established constants gives the selected equations. Setting x=0 gives (0,-7) for q-30873 and (0,10.5) for q-30269. For q-7239, c=-1 and k=2-(-1)=3; for q-7241, c=4 and k=5.5-4=1.5. In grid units, q-120257 has a=(6,0), b=(-3,-2), c=(3,4), so c+2b=(-3,0)=-a/2. q-70148 has a=(4,0), b=(-4,4), c=(-6,-4), so c+b=(-10,0)=-2.5a. For q-42669, OW=u+(2/9)(v-u)=(7/9)u+(2/9)v. Finally, q-27477 is decreasing with intercept (0,9/10) and asymptote y=-1/10, matching current option 1 and its own worked solution. No answer disagreement is present; no submitted-grade evidence was supplied.",
